<p>Vietnam opened polls on Sunday for elections to its 500-seat 16th National Assembly, with voters choosing from a candidate list heavily dominated by the ruling Communist Party of Vietnam, which fielded nearly 93% of those standing. The vote comes in the one-party Southeast Asian state, where the ruling party dominates the ballot rather than facing a competitive multi-party field.</p><img src='https://kagiproxy.com/img/XL1pZlmaxGRvnA5uFGKO-DZxpq1tHBwmLgl0I-BjOZfPsmCdIgeDDMTpZ7pMjtIVNXy8F4iJJoBAyV274KrP_vw4EndSe9hIL2bhB4nbbtTaOgnT_ZE5HkKiXN_P3s-pCZ4aQP8mm3uKzS1bH2Xtcs5JYZG_zHwK6PgPhNzD1U6FGsAfmtZWbeNFqKk_DJ0W6blBy4Hc8MAdVB8cAUvDXVLMOAZ_pCyENE9RHNAuU-4' alt='Voters take part in Vietnam’s parliamentary election.' /><br /><h3>Highlights:</h3><ul><li>Political climate: The Hindu described Vietnam as a repressive one-party state that often jails critics, underscoring the tight limits on dissent.</li><li>Population scale: The election is taking place in a country of about 100 million people, making it a nationwide exercise despite limited political competition.</li><li>Economic contrast: The Hindu also framed Vietnam as an economic success story, with growth of 8% last year.</li></ul><h3>Perspectives:</h3><ul><li>Reuters: Reuters focused on the legal structure of the vote, noting that the Communist Party of Vietnam is the only legal party contesting the election. (<a href='https://www.reuters.com/world/asia-pacific/communist-party-fields-nearly-93-candidates-vietnam-holds-parliament-elections-2026-03-15/'>Reuters</a>)</li><li>Al Jazeera: Al Jazeera highlighted the makeup of the ballot, reporting that nearly 93% of candidates were fielded by the governing Communist Party. (<a href='https://www.aljazeera.com/news/2026/3/15/vietnam-holds-general-election-93-candidates-from-ruling-communist-party'>Al Jazeera</a>)</li><li>Firstpost: Firstpost emphasized the institutional role of the National Assembly, describing it as the country’s top legislative body that mainly ratifies decisions the ruling party has already made. (<a href='https://www.firstpost.com/world/vietnam-a-repressive-one-party-nation-holds-parliamentary-elections-13989613.html'>Firstpost</a>)</li></ul><h3>Sources:</h3><ul><li><a href='https://www.dw.com/en/vietnam-polls-open-in-one-party-election/a-76364475'>Vietnam: Polls open in one-party election</a> - dw.com</li><li><a href='https://www.firstpost.com/world/vietnam-a-repressive-one-party-nation-holds-parliamentary-elections-13989613.html'>Vietnam: A repressive one-party nation holds parliamentary elections</a> - firstpost.com</li><li><a href='https://www.aljazeera.com/news/2026/3/15/vietnam-holds-general-election-93-candidates-from-ruling-communist-party'>Vietnam holds general election, 93% candidates from ruling Communist Party</a> - aljazeera.com</li><li><a href='https://www.thehindu.com/news/international/vietnam-single-party-legislative-election/article70745637.ece'>Polls open as single-party Vietnam holds legislative election</a> - thehindu.com</li><li><a href='https://www.reuters.com/world/asia-pacific/communist-party-fields-nearly-93-candidates-vietnam-holds-parliament-elections-2026-03-15/'>Vietnamese people vote to elect the 500 members of the 16th National Assembly. The sole legal party of Vietnam contesting the election is the Communist Party of Vietnam.</a> - reuters.com</li></ul>